[04:24:20] STORY-APP-008 is done.
[04:24:20] ## What changed
[04:24:20] **Established the existing behavior first** (AC 1) — the two timers are not the same sequence:
[04:24:20] | | `CraftingProfitView` | `CraftingDiscoveryView` |
[04:24:20] |---|---|---|
[04:24:20] | Interval | 90s | 120s |
[04:24:20] | Sync | `syncAccountMaterials`, `syncAccountRecipes` | `syncAccountBank`, `syncAccountMaterials`, `syncAccountRecipes`, `syncCharactersCraftingAndRecipes` |
[04:24:20] | Success | countdown reset → status text → `reloadTable.run()` | same + `"Last refresh: just now"` |
[04:24:20] | Failure | `printStackTrace`, reset anyway, status text, **no** reload | same + `"Last refresh: FAILED"` |
[04:24:20] Discovery's sequence is byte-for-byte the Sync Account one, so it reuses `AccountRefreshService.refreshAll()`. Profit's is genuinely narrower — substituting `refreshAll()` would have added a bank sync and a full character sync that timer never performed — so the service gained a second named operation, `refreshMaterialsAndRecipes()`, following `TradingPostPriceRefreshService`'s existing one-service/two-variant precedent. No new gateway: `sync.AccountRefreshGateway` already exposed both methods.
[04:24:20] Scheduler, cadence, shutdown-on-reopen, countdown label and reset, `Platform.runLater` updates and the post-refresh reload all stayed in the views. Each view gained a four-argument `show(...)` overload (the three-argument one forwards, so `Gw2App` and the existing TP-refresh ITs are untouched) and publishes its refresh `Runnable` in a package-private static `autoRefreshTask` field — that's the seam the UI checks use to run the scheduler's real task without waiting out a 90/120-second countdown. Neither view imports `sync.*` any more; no default-package class does.
[04:24:20] ## Tests
[04:24:20] - `application.AccountRefreshServiceTest` — 7 tests (3 new: materials-then-recipes order with bank/character steps asserted *absent*, plus both failure short-circuits). Pass.
[04:24:20] - `CraftingProfitViewAutoRefreshIT` / `CraftingDiscoveryViewAutoRefreshIT` (new, 2 each) — exactly-once off-FX-thread delegation to the correct variant, the other variant never called, reload/status/`Last refresh` on success and failure, scope+search+sort preserved. Pass.
[04:24:20] - Regressions: both TP-refresh ITs, `CraftingProfitViewRefreshPreservationIT`, `Gw2AppSyncAccountIT`. Pass.
[04:24:20] - Full default suite: **143 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors.**
[04:24:20] ## Limitations
[04:24:20] The real countdown interval and per-second label tick aren't exercised — tests drive the scheduler's task directly, so the countdown-reset lines are covered by reading, not assertion. The `"🔄 Auto-refreshed Bank + Materials"` success text is still unpollable (the following reload overwrites it in the same JavaFX pulse) — the pre-existing quirk STORY-APP-006 documented, unchanged here. Phase 3/milestone completion is not claimed; `BankView`/`MaterialsView` remain a separate bypass.
[04:24:20] Docs: `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` §5.4 and §6 (boundary count unchanged — no tenth service). Story file, `BACKLOG.md` and `CLAUDE_RESULT.md` updated; committed as `8a1fbbe`. Note that `docs/CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` and `agent/stories/BACKLOG.md` carried uncommitted edits from earlier stories, so those went into this commit too.
