[09:18:07] ## What changed
[09:18:07] **New application boundary** — `application/CharacterSelectionService.java` with two named operations, `getCraftingCharacterOptions()` and `getCharacterNames()`, delegating to the unchanged `CharacterRepository` reads. It follows the `BankContentsService`/`MaterialStorageService` pattern: no JavaFX, no calculation, one collaborator behind a constructor seam, `SQLException` propagated unchanged. One shared service rather than extra methods on the two calculation services, since both views need the same read and it must not be coupled to a reload.
[09:18:07] **Both crafting views** lost their `repo.CharacterRepository` instance and now call the injected service; each gained a five-arg `show(..., CharacterSelectionService)` overload with the four-arg one forwarding, so `Gw2App` is untouched. After this story no view in the codebase constructs a `repo.*` repository.
[09:18:07] I recorded all three call sites' behavior first (full table in the story Result) and preserved it verbatim — including the three deliberately *different* failure presentations (Profit silent, Discovery's "❌ Failed loading characters", Discovery's silent name-load failure) and Discovery's previous-selection branch that is unreachable in production today. None were "improved".
[09:18:07] ## Tests
