[09:28:19] ## What changed
[09:28:19] `src/main/java/CraftingProfitView.java` only — presentation no longer owns total profit. The value now flows unbroken: `CraftingPlanner` → `CraftResult.totalProfitCopper` → `UiRow.totalProfitCopper` → `CraftRow.totalProfitCopper` → column + both sort paths.
[09:28:19] 1. `CraftRow` gained a `totalProfitCopper` constructor parameter that finally sets the already-declared-but-never-assigned property. The row-construction loop moved verbatim out of `show(...)` into a package-private `toCraftRow(UiRow)` so the mapping is checkable without a window (`CraftingProfitView.java:947`).
[09:28:19] 2. The "Total profit" column binds to `totalProfitCopperProperty()` — the same one-line form the neighbouring "Profit per craft" column already used — replacing `new SimpleIntegerProperty(craftable * profitPer)` (`CraftingProfitView.java:593`).
[09:28:19] 3. The sort-box `switch` moved into a package-private `rowComparator(String)`; its "Total profit" case and default fallback now both use `comparingInt(CraftRow::getTotalProfitCopper).reversed()` (`CraftingProfitView.java:971`). The other three cases are unchanged, including "Total sell value"'s own `revenue × count` product (a different figure, out of scope).
[09:28:19] Filter, stable descending sort, tie order, `profitCell()` currency formatting and blocked-row "Unavailable" rendering are untouched; no domain code changed.
[09:28:19] ## Tests
[09:28:19] - New `CraftingProfitTotalProfitPresentationTest` (5 tests, plain JUnit): rows carry supplied totals deliberately unequal to `craftableCount × profitCopper`, so a recomputation reverses the expected order and fails. That divergence is only constructible with hand-built rows — the domain's own total *is* that product, which is why the review saw no numeric divergence and why a DB fixture would prove nothing.
[09:28:19] - `./mvnw test` on the final tree: `Tests run: 170, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.
[09:28:19] - Real-view re-runs: `CraftingProfitViewSmokeIT` + `CraftingProfitViewBlockedRowIT` (2 tests, 0 failures) and `CraftingProfitViewRefreshPreservationIT` (1 test, 0 failures).
[09:28:19] ## Docs
[09:28:19] `KNOWN_PROBLEMS.md` §4.4's closing paragraph now records the total-profit portion resolved with its verification, and §10's CH-E2 line records both halves resolved — the selector paragraph was left as-is, since APP-010 had already resolved it and nothing unresolved remained there. `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` §4's bullet claiming the duplication "remains open" was corrected at its owner. Story file, `CLAUDE_RESULT.md` and the BACKLOG entry updated; no milestone or phase transition declared.
[09:28:19] **Remaining uncertainty:** the column-to-property binding itself is covered by reading rather than a live `TableColumn` assertion — the ITs confirm rendering but cannot distinguish the two formulas, for the reason above. No `CraftRow` construction site exists outside `toCraftRow(...)`.
