[20:19:27] Story complete. Summary:
[20:19:27] ## What changed
[20:19:27] **`POST /api/crafting/discovery`** exposes the existing `application.CraftingDiscoveryService` on the Spring Boot runtime STORY-API-001 established. No JavaFX file and no `pom.xml` change.
[20:19:27] **Contract** (documented in `docs/CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` §5.6): body and scope required — `discipline`, `characterName`, `rating`, always mapped to `DiscChoice.charDiscipline(...)`, because Discovery is individual-character only and the JavaFX selector offers nothing else. `rating` is *required rather than defaulted* since it drives the `minRating` filter and a silent 0 would answer with an emptier result than asked for. `inventoryCharacterName` is separate and optional; blank/omitted reaches the service as null, preserving its own unfiltered-inventory fallback. Settings default to Discovery's own opening state (buying **on**, 20g) — not Profit's; `dailyBuyInsteadOfCraft` stays a fixed false, echoed but not accepted. Seven validation rules reject before any service is constructed; nothing-left-to-discover is an empty 200.
[20:19:27] **Shared boundary change** (the one the story's Required Tests anticipated): Discovery's row is the identical projection of the identical domain objects, so Profit's nested row/missing/quote records were promoted to shared `web.dto.CraftingRowDto`/`MissingItemDto`/`TradingPostQuoteDto`, copying moved to `web.CraftingRowMapper`, and `ApiExceptionHandler` now covers both controllers. JSON field names byte-identical; the only visible Profit change is two generalized human-readable failure messages — codes and statuses unchanged.
[20:19:27] ## §23/UD-007 choice: synchronous, by measurement
[20:19:27] Real PostgreSQL, real embedded server, scope read from the database. Page-load-equivalent scope (672 rows, 721 KB): first **1304 ms**, repeats 628/484/329 ms. One warm request per *other* synced combination — all 19, 0–1085 rows, up to 1.1 MB — **258–515 ms**. A second full run agreed. Comfortably inside a normal request, so synchronous: no task, no status endpoint, no competing mechanism.
[20:19:27] ## Tests
[20:19:27] - `./mvnw test` — **209 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors** (189 pre-existing + 20 new contract tests).
[20:19:27] - Discovery real-DB equivalence: 672 rows match the in-process call field by field, with and without an inventory character.
[20:19:27] - **Profit real-DB equivalence re-run: 3151 rows still equivalent** — that, not the contract tests, is what proves the shared-mapper refactor preserved values and not just field names.
[20:19:27] - `uiverify.CraftingDiscoveryView{BlockedRow,RefreshPreservation}IT` both pass on the final tree.
[20:19:27] ## Remaining uncertainty
[20:19:27] The resolution tree is not on this route (the service builds it lazily per row — needs a detail endpoint), there is still no authentication on either route, and the measurement is backend request time only, so it says nothing about §33's seven-second page budget. Milestone completion is not declared; the Phase 4 health review stays open.
